"""
The database of a test: SQLite in memory, or the PostgreSQL of the test server when
the environment says so, so that one test file runs on both backends.

- WOLLY_DB unset or "sqlite": an SQLite database in memory.
- WOLLY_DB "postgres": a connection to the server named by HILDE_PG_HOST, HILDE_PG_PORT,
  HILDE_PG_DATABASE, HILDE_PG_USER, HILDE_PG_PASSWORD and HILDE_PG_CA (scripts/db/server.sh
  makes the server and prints them), over TLS with the password, and the schema public of
  the database dropped and made again, so that no test sees the tables of another.
- A variable that is missing on a run with postgres stops the test: it never falls back to
  SQLite, since that would count a run on PostgreSQL that did not happen.
- A database that does not keep its text as UTF8 stops the test as well: the server is
  started with LC_ALL=C.UTF-8, since initdb in the C locale makes SQL_ASCII.

    case openTestDatabase() of
        when Right(right as opened: Database[Writing]) do
            ...
            closeDatabase(opened);
        when Left(left as error: DbError) do
            ...
    end case;
"""
import Standard.Database (
    Database,
    Writing,
    DbError
);

module Wolly.TestDb is
    """
    The database of a test, as the environment says.
    No contract: the outcome is the result of I/O.
    """
    function openTestDatabase(): Either[DbError, Database[Writing]];
end module.
